# Byte-stability for test fixtures and binary assets.
#
# Several suites byte-compare these files (canonical manifests, MPC streams,
# oracle vectors, fuzz corpora, MPAK containers), so they must check out
# identically on every platform regardless of `core.autocrlf`. Without this,
# a Windows checkout silently appends CR bytes and byte-indexed tests
# (e.g. the fuzz-lite truncation corpus) diverge from the reference.
/fixtures/**            -text
/tests/**/data/**       -text
/crates/**/tests/data/** -text
/fuzz/corpus/**         -text
*.mpc                   -text
*.mpak                  -text
*.db                    -text
*.f32le                 -text
